"""037.md batch T: deepen vv 80, 115, 116, 129 (the four shortest sections).

All four bodies were verified correct against their own verses before rewriting,
so this is depth work only, not repair. Each is written on a different portion of
the shared apparatus notes:

  v115 takes the two readings of "the great distress" from the shared [114-115]
       note, leaving v114 (rebuilt in batch R) the reading of the favour itself.
  v116 takes the [116] note on the scope of the pronouns, which no neighbour
       covers.
  v129 takes the blessing-among-later-generations and the pointer to 37:77-79,
       leaving v130 (rebuilt in batch P) the Ilyas / Ilyasin name discussion.
  v80  takes 29:69c on "the virtuous" and the reward-of-goodness principle at
       42:23 and 55:60; the parallel list at 6:84 / 12:22 / 28:14 / 77:44 was
       already in the existing body and is retained rather than repeated.

Guards: no verbatim re-quote of the verse in the opening prose; no verbatim
repeat of blockquote wording in the prose above it; echo the verse's own
distinctive vocabulary; paragraphs distinct so duprate stays under 0.025.
"""

